WEBVTT

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:01.621
And Facebook transmitting the photos,

00:01:01.621 --> 00:01:02.829
messages and stories

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:05.996
of over 1.23 billion people.

00:01:05.996 --> 00:01:08.746
That's almost half of the Internet population,

00:01:08.746 --> 00:01:11.413
and a sixth of humanity.

00:01:11.413 --> 00:01:12.413
These are some of the products

00:01:12.413 --> 00:01:15.163
that I've helped design over the course of my career,

00:01:15.163 --> 00:01:17.288
and their scale is so massive

00:01:17.288 --> 00:01:19.163
that they've produced unprecedented

00:01:19.163 --> 00:01:21.038
design challenges.

00:01:21.038 --> 00:01:23.371
But what is really hard

00:01:23.371 --> 00:01:26.121
about designing at scale is this:

00:01:26.121 --> 00:01:27.954
It's hard in part because

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:30.871
it requires a combination of two things,